1
00:00:02,160 --> 00:00:04,030
Previously on The Big Bang Theory...

2
00:00:04,470 --> 00:00:06,120
Can I have your attention, please?

3
00:00:07,650 --> 00:00:09,730
We're all here tonight

4
00:00:09,730 --> 00:00:11,740
because we have no one to be with.

5
00:00:11,940 --> 00:00:14,970
We've got to stop defining our self-worth

6
00:00:14,970 --> 00:00:18,340
by whether or not we're in a relationship.

7
00:00:18,340 --> 00:00:20,840
We are a community,

8
00:00:20,840 --> 00:00:23,330
and as long as we have each other,

9
00:00:23,330 --> 00:00:25,490
we're never truly alone.

10
00:00:30,120 --> 00:00:32,190
That was cool. What you said.

11
00:00:32,190 --> 00:00:33,060
Thank you.

12
00:00:37,810 --> 00:00:39,150
Uh... would you like to, uh...

13
00:00:39,150 --> 00:00:41,610
get a cup... a cup of coffee...?

14
00:00:42,340 --> 00:00:43,470
Okay.

15
00:00:49,000 --> 00:00:50,830
Later, losers!

16
00:00:54,110 --> 00:00:57,090
So then I went to Cambridge, which was wonderful

17
00:00:57,090 --> 00:00:57,340
not only because it's a good school

18
00:00:57,350 --> 00:01:01,580
but because it totally looks like Hogwarts.

19
00:01:02,480 --> 00:01:04,670
That's where I fell in love with astronomy,

20
00:01:04,670 --> 00:01:07,180
and now I'm an astrophysicist at Caltech,

21
00:01:07,180 --> 00:01:09,200
so I guess you could say, uh,

22
00:01:09,200 --> 00:01:12,700
Raj is my name and stars are my game.

23
00:01:13,400 --> 00:01:15,820
And rhyming is also my game.

24
00:01:16,380 --> 00:01:19,420
So, uh, two games.

25
00:01:19,950 --> 00:01:21,530
Uh, anyway, that-that's enough about me.

26
00:01:21,530 --> 00:01:23,910
I want to hear everything about you.

27
00:01:24,820 --> 00:01:26,960
I have to go to the bathroom.

28
00:01:27,530 --> 00:01:29,350
I go to the bathroom, too.

29
00:01:29,900 --> 00:01:32,280
Sometimes more frequently than I care to admit.

30
00:01:32,280 --> 00:01:35,150
Oh, I've had it checked out, it's nothing.

31
00:01:38,650 --> 00:01:40,450
This is going great!

32
00:01:42,420 --> 00:01:44,670
Can I have a refill on my chai tea?

33
00:01:45,980 --> 00:01:47,100
Yes...

34
00:01:47,100 --> 00:01:49,290
I have a good feeling about this.

35
00:01:52,080 --> 00:01:53,960
I should have bought condoms.

36
00:02:22,550 --> 00:02:25,650
Hello, I'm Dr. Sheldon Cooper.

37
00:02:26,280 --> 00:02:30,080
Welcome to Sheldon Cooper Presents: Fun with Flags.

38
00:02:33,240 --> 00:02:35,830
My apologies that this episode is coming late.

39
00:02:35,830 --> 00:02:39,530
I did shoot one last week, in honor of Black History Month,

40
00:02:39,530 --> 00:02:41,180
but I was informed by my roommate

41
00:02:41,180 --> 00:02:44,160
that my spot-on portrayal of George Washington Carver

42
00:02:44,160 --> 00:02:46,990
could be considered "wildly racist."

43
00:02:49,490 --> 00:02:51,050
My heart goes out to the members

44
00:02:51,050 --> 00:02:52,900
of the African-American community,

45
00:02:52,900 --> 00:02:56,190
who, like me, have been kept down by The Man.

46
00:02:58,130 --> 00:03:02,470
Now, Fun with Flags is not just for the flag aficionado;

47
00:03:02,470 --> 00:03:04,890
it's also for the flag novice,

48
00:03:04,890 --> 00:03:06,360
so, to help me with that,

49
00:03:06,360 --> 00:03:09,760
please welcome my friend, neighbor, and flag virgin--

50
00:03:09,760 --> 00:03:11,940
yeah, not a real virgin.

51
00:03:13,600 --> 00:03:15,790
She's had coitus many times.

52
00:03:17,690 --> 00:03:20,950
Sometimes within earshot of this flag enthusiast.

53
00:03:21,890 --> 00:03:24,330
Once while he was trying to watch The Incredibles.

54
00:03:25,600 --> 00:03:27,050
Penny.

55
00:03:28,690 --> 00:03:30,190
Hello.

56
00:03:30,190 --> 00:03:31,760
So, Penny, I understand

57
00:03:31,760 --> 00:03:34,120
you would like to learn more about flags.

58
00:03:34,120 --> 00:03:35,560
Yeah, I can't tell you how many times

59
00:03:35,560 --> 00:03:37,670
I've been at a party where everyone's talking about flags

60
00:03:37,670 --> 00:03:39,380
and I just couldn't join in. Yeah.

61
00:03:40,530 --> 00:03:43,020
Well, you came to the right place.

62
00:03:46,110 --> 00:03:48,240
Uh, I'm sorry, can we just pause for a minute?

63
00:03:50,680 --> 00:03:51,720
What's wrong?

64
00:03:51,720 --> 00:03:53,540
I just think it might look more natural

65
00:03:53,540 --> 00:03:55,680
if you talked to me instead of the camera,

66
00:03:55,680 --> 00:03:57,460
you know, like, like a real conversation.

67
00:03:57,460 --> 00:03:59,810
It's something we work on in my acting class.

68
00:03:59,810 --> 00:04:01,250
Interesting.

69
00:04:01,250 --> 00:04:03,720
A few people in the comments section have said

70
00:04:03,720 --> 00:04:06,020
that my delivery is robotic.

71
00:04:07,940 --> 00:04:10,520
Perhaps that isn't the compliment it sounds like.

72
00:04:11,660 --> 00:04:13,150
Yeah, let's try it again, and maybe, this time,

73
00:04:13,150 --> 00:04:15,250
you could work on your body language a bit.

74
00:04:15,250 --> 00:04:17,060
You know, when you're all hunched like that,

75
00:04:17,060 --> 00:04:18,400
you're shutting the audience out,

76
00:04:18,400 --> 00:04:20,740
but when you're relaxed and open,

77
00:04:20,740 --> 00:04:22,550
you're inviting them in.

78
00:04:22,550 --> 00:04:24,510
Right.

79
00:04:25,200 --> 00:04:27,280
And which one do I want?

80
00:04:28,620 --> 00:04:30,020
Let's try open.

81
00:04:30,020 --> 00:04:31,740
If our friend, the flag, has taught me anything,

82
00:04:31,740 --> 00:04:34,000
it's to go where the wind takes you.

83
00:04:34,000 --> 00:04:37,520
As long as you remain firmly attached to a rigid pole.

84
00:04:38,410 --> 00:04:40,330
And... action.

85
00:04:50,410 --> 00:04:52,000
So, Penny...

86
00:04:52,000 --> 00:04:55,970
what sort of flag questions keep you awake at night?

87
00:05:00,860 --> 00:05:03,210
Um, well, I'm from Nebraska.

88
00:05:03,210 --> 00:05:05,650
So what can you tell me about the state flag?

89
00:05:05,650 --> 00:05:07,450
Gosh, Penny...

90
00:05:08,770 --> 00:05:10,260
what'd you have for breakfast?

91
00:05:10,260 --> 00:05:13,190
A big glass of good question juice?

92
00:05:14,210 --> 00:05:17,580
The Nebraska state flag is simply the state seal

93
00:05:17,580 --> 00:05:19,670
on a field of blue.

94
00:05:32,180 --> 00:05:34,290
Spread your legs; invite them in.

95
00:05:39,810 --> 00:05:41,400
I'm telling you, something's wrong.

96
00:05:41,400 --> 00:05:44,010
I can always feel it when Raj is in trouble.

97
00:05:44,010 --> 00:05:46,470
Geez, how close were you guys before we got married?

98
00:05:46,470 --> 00:05:48,710
Don't look under that rock.

99
00:05:50,270 --> 00:05:52,260
- Raj, you okay? - You in there?

100
00:05:52,260 --> 00:05:53,470
Go away!

101
00:05:54,380 --> 00:05:55,730
Come on, buddy, open up.

102
00:05:55,730 --> 00:05:57,330
We're worried about you.

103
00:05:57,330 --> 00:05:59,380
Oh, just because I stopped going to work

104
00:05:59,380 --> 00:06:02,580
and answering my phone you think something bad happened?

105
00:06:03,530 --> 00:06:05,830
Maybe something good happened.

106
00:06:05,830 --> 00:06:07,810
Did something good happen?

107
00:06:07,810 --> 00:06:08,430
Of course not!

108
00:06:08,430 --> 00:06:10,540
Nothing good ever happens!

109
00:06:18,070 --> 00:06:18,740
What?

110
00:06:18,740 --> 00:06:20,910
Nope, just-just... whoa.

111
00:06:27,000 --> 00:06:29,170
It smells pretty ripe in here.

112
00:06:30,870 --> 00:06:33,580
You kind feel it in your eyes.

113
00:06:34,450 --> 00:06:36,220
Raj, what's going on?

114
00:06:36,220 --> 00:06:39,490
I was humiliated by yet another woman.

115
00:06:39,490 --> 00:06:41,210
You didn't kill her and chop her up--

116
00:06:41,210 --> 00:06:42,910
that's not what we're smelling, right?

117
00:06:43,630 --> 00:06:44,770
No.

118
00:06:45,260 --> 00:06:46,580
I took her for coffee,

119
00:06:46,580 --> 00:06:48,620
and she snuck out the bathroom window

120
00:06:48,620 --> 00:06:49,930
to get away from me.

121
00:06:49,930 --> 00:06:51,810
Oh, you poor baby.

122
00:06:51,810 --> 00:06:53,100
I went and looked.

123
00:06:53,100 --> 00:06:55,530
It was a high and tiny window.

124
00:06:56,820 --> 00:06:59,340
She must have been very motivated.

125
00:06:59,950 --> 00:07:02,730
I'm sorry. That's awful, but come on.

126
00:07:02,730 --> 00:07:04,660
you got to shake it off.

127
00:07:04,660 --> 00:07:05,740
Yeah, you can't stay in your apartment

128
00:07:05,740 --> 00:07:07,270
for the rest of your life.

129
00:07:07,270 --> 00:07:08,550
Why not?

130
00:07:08,550 --> 00:07:10,700
With online shopping and overnight delivery,

131
00:07:10,700 --> 00:07:12,460
I can get anything I want.

132
00:07:12,780 --> 00:07:13,370
Look,

133
00:07:13,370 --> 00:07:16,560
I just ordered a case of Dinty Moore beef stew

134
00:07:16,560 --> 00:07:18,980
and two live lobsters on Amazon.

135
00:07:19,940 --> 00:07:21,010
Lobsters overnight?

136
00:07:21,010 --> 00:07:22,660
Oh, you're kidding. Let me see.

137
00:07:22,660 --> 00:07:24,180
Well, I'll be.

138
00:07:24,180 --> 00:07:25,520
Look, you can throw in a couple steaks

139
00:07:25,520 --> 00:07:27,360
and have a surf and turf.

140
00:07:28,280 --> 00:07:29,650
The surf and turf sounds good.

141
00:07:29,650 --> 00:07:31,230
See if they corn on the cob.

142
00:07:32,930 --> 00:07:33,740
Guys!

143
00:07:33,740 --> 00:07:34,970
We're trying to get him out of here,

144
00:07:34,970 --> 00:07:36,980
not you in.

145
00:07:37,450 --> 00:07:38,850
You're wasting your time.

146
00:07:38,850 --> 00:07:41,560
Just please, leave me alone.

147
00:07:45,980 --> 00:07:47,110
Now what?

148
00:07:47,110 --> 00:07:48,690
I don't know.

149
00:07:49,380 --> 00:07:52,290
We could go to Red Lobster and talk about it.

150
00:07:54,070 --> 00:07:55,030
We're all thinking it.

151
00:07:55,030 --> 00:07:57,960
I just had the decency to wait for him to leave.

152
00:08:05,320 --> 00:08:06,660
Hello, Sheldon.

153
00:08:06,660 --> 00:08:07,890
Hello.

154
00:08:07,890 --> 00:08:08,900
How's the final stage of

155
00:08:08,900 --> 00:08:11,270
your nicotine addiction study going?

156
00:08:12,000 --> 00:08:12,830
Fine.

157
00:08:13,960 --> 00:08:14,780
Just hold on.

158
00:08:14,780 --> 00:08:16,860
Mommy's on the phone!

159
00:08:19,170 --> 00:08:19,990
Sorry.

160
00:08:19,990 --> 00:08:22,250
We've cut the monkeys down to one cigarette a day,

161
00:08:22,250 --> 00:08:24,210
so things are a little intense.

162
00:08:25,460 --> 00:08:27,710
Makes me miss my marijuana-abusing flatworms.

163
00:08:27,710 --> 00:08:29,620
Those guys were mellow.

164
00:08:30,910 --> 00:08:32,030
Good news.

165
00:08:32,030 --> 00:08:35,150
Uh, the latest episode of Fun with Flags is online.

166
00:08:35,150 --> 00:08:37,090
Oh, that's right. How'd it go with Penny?

167
00:08:37,090 --> 00:08:39,100
Much better than I expected.

168
00:08:39,100 --> 00:08:41,360
She even gave me some helpful tips

169
00:08:41,360 --> 00:08:43,700
about acting and body language.

170
00:08:43,700 --> 00:08:45,020
Watch.

171
00:08:46,340 --> 00:08:48,190
Welcome to my world.

172
00:08:49,630 --> 00:08:51,850
Not welcome to my world.

173
00:08:53,040 --> 00:08:53,930
Welcome.

174
00:08:53,930 --> 00:08:55,460
Not welcome.

175
00:08:56,850 --> 00:08:58,830
Subtle, but powerful.

176
00:08:58,830 --> 00:08:59,700
I know.

177
00:08:59,700 --> 00:09:02,090
I'm still learning to control it.

178
00:09:02,970 --> 00:09:05,380
Did you tell Penny how helpful she was?

179
00:09:05,380 --> 00:09:07,380
Why would I do that?

180
00:09:07,380 --> 00:09:10,150
Because she's your friend, and she did a nice job.

181
00:09:10,150 --> 00:09:12,580
I'm sure she'd like to hear it.

182
00:09:13,560 --> 00:09:14,930
All right.

183
00:09:15,770 --> 00:09:17,780
I didn't mean now. Hello?

184
00:09:20,190 --> 00:09:21,530
Yeah, yeah, you want a cigarette.

185
00:09:21,530 --> 00:09:22,810
Well, I'd like a normal boyfriend.

186
00:09:22,810 --> 00:09:24,520
Deal with it.

187
00:09:27,330 --> 00:09:29,210
Oh, hi. What's up?

188
00:09:32,130 --> 00:09:33,190
You need me to shut the door

189
00:09:33,190 --> 00:09:35,270
so you can do your knocking thing?

190
00:09:36,990 --> 00:09:37,660
No.

191
00:09:37,660 --> 00:09:39,790
- I didn't start yet; it's fine. - Okay.

192
00:09:40,410 --> 00:09:41,420
So, what do you need?

193
00:09:41,420 --> 00:09:43,170
Well, I was thinking

194
00:09:43,170 --> 00:09:45,810
about you helping me out last night...

195
00:09:46,720 --> 00:09:47,610
Penny.

196
00:09:50,050 --> 00:09:53,000
And I just wanted to tell you...

197
00:09:53,000 --> 00:09:54,510
Penny.

198
00:09:55,690 --> 00:09:58,070
...that the answer to the question,

199
00:09:58,070 --> 00:10:00,930
"who did a great job?" is you.

200
00:10:01,650 --> 00:10:02,740
Penny.

201
00:10:04,570 --> 00:10:06,100
- Really? -Yes.

202
00:10:06,100 --> 00:10:08,180
You were very natural in front of the camera,

203
00:10:08,180 --> 00:10:11,250
and I found your suggestions extremely helpful.

204
00:10:11,720 --> 00:10:14,230
Aw, sweetie, you just made my day.

205
00:10:14,800 --> 00:10:16,260
Okay.

206
00:10:17,250 --> 00:10:19,680
Hey, my acting class is putting on a play Friday night.

207
00:10:19,680 --> 00:10:21,640
I could put you and Amy on the guest list.

208
00:10:21,640 --> 00:10:22,760
Oh, that sounds terrible.

209
00:10:22,760 --> 00:10:24,770
Why would I want to do that?

210
00:10:26,520 --> 00:10:27,860
That's right.

211
00:10:27,860 --> 00:10:31,400
They're no good without the lighter.

212
00:10:32,160 --> 00:10:34,740
Well, so much for your advice on complimenting Penny.

213
00:10:34,740 --> 00:10:35,950
Why? What happened?

214
00:10:35,950 --> 00:10:37,070
She tried to rope us into going

215
00:10:37,070 --> 00:10:39,600
to her acting class to see a play.

216
00:10:39,600 --> 00:10:40,240
Don't worry.

217
00:10:40,240 --> 00:10:41,380
Luckily, I had the good sense

218
00:10:41,380 --> 00:10:43,440
to drown that kitten in the river.

219
00:10:46,090 --> 00:10:48,220
Sheldon, that's very rude.

220
00:10:48,220 --> 00:10:49,480
She helped you with your show.

221
00:10:49,480 --> 00:10:51,160
The right thing to do is reciprocate

222
00:10:51,160 --> 00:10:53,760
by going to see her play.

223
00:10:53,760 --> 00:10:56,420
Oh, so many crazy rules.

224
00:10:59,670 --> 00:11:02,530
That better be Tootsie Rolls you're throwing at me!

225
00:11:05,540 --> 00:11:07,790
Penny. Penny.

226
00:11:08,390 --> 00:11:09,110
Penny.

227
00:11:09,110 --> 00:11:11,040
Oh yeah, much better.

228
00:11:12,880 --> 00:11:13,760
What?

229
00:11:13,760 --> 00:11:15,200
Amy pointed out to me

230
00:11:15,200 --> 00:11:17,700
that since you did something nice for me,

231
00:11:17,700 --> 00:11:20,730
I'm obligated to do something nice for you.

232
00:11:20,730 --> 00:11:21,510
So...

233
00:11:21,510 --> 00:11:25,060
yes, I'll go to your dopey play.

234
00:11:25,890 --> 00:11:27,430
Hey, I don't want you to go anymore.

235
00:11:27,430 --> 00:11:28,430
Why not?

236
00:11:28,430 --> 00:11:29,710
You should go 'cause you want to go,

237
00:11:29,710 --> 00:11:31,050
not because you have to.

238
00:11:31,050 --> 00:11:34,040
Oh, Dear Lord, more rules? Where does it stop?

239
00:11:34,670 --> 00:11:36,900
Can I want to go

240
00:11:36,900 --> 00:11:40,210
because I have to want to go?

241
00:11:40,210 --> 00:11:41,570
Okay. Do whatever you want.

242
00:11:41,570 --> 00:11:43,220
Yeah, but now, wait.

243
00:11:43,220 --> 00:11:45,600
Do whatever I want...

244
00:11:45,600 --> 00:11:48,080
or whatever I have to want?

245
00:11:49,250 --> 00:11:51,760
Oh, for God's sake, just come to the play.

246
00:11:51,760 --> 00:11:52,870
All right.

247
00:11:52,870 --> 00:11:56,270
I don't want to, but at least that makes sense.

248
00:12:02,090 --> 00:12:05,610
You know, I haven't seen Raj in several days.

249
00:12:05,610 --> 00:12:07,940
Is he no longer a part of our social group?

250
00:12:08,750 --> 00:12:12,380
And if so, should we be interviewing for a replacement?

251
00:12:13,350 --> 00:12:16,290
Perhaps, this time, we go Latin.

252
00:12:19,510 --> 00:12:22,680
He's just decided he's never leaving his apartment again.

253
00:12:22,680 --> 00:12:24,070
Oh, brilliant.

254
00:12:24,070 --> 00:12:26,140
I've been itching to pull that trigger.

255
00:12:27,190 --> 00:12:30,930
He's upset because he can't get anywhere with women.

256
00:12:31,680 --> 00:12:34,300
Would it help if I gave him some pointers?

257
00:12:38,580 --> 00:12:39,900
I'm just funnin' ya.

258
00:12:45,800 --> 00:12:46,650
Hi.

259
00:12:46,650 --> 00:12:48,140
I don't know if you remember me,

260
00:12:48,140 --> 00:12:50,520
but I was here the other night at your party.

261
00:12:50,520 --> 00:12:53,390
Oh, yeah, you left with Raj.

262
00:12:53,390 --> 00:12:55,090
Uh, yeah.

263
00:12:55,090 --> 00:12:56,700
You're the one?

264
00:12:56,700 --> 00:12:58,330
Okay, let me tell you something.

265
00:12:58,330 --> 00:13:00,010
That guy you blew off

266
00:13:00,010 --> 00:13:02,640
happens to be my best friend.

267
00:13:02,640 --> 00:13:04,380
Okay? He was devastated.

268
00:13:04,380 --> 00:13:05,640
Sorry.

269
00:13:06,280 --> 00:13:08,270
Can you just give him this?

270
00:13:08,820 --> 00:13:10,080
Okay.

271
00:13:10,080 --> 00:13:11,010
But I gotta warn you,

272
00:13:11,010 --> 00:13:14,370
Raj is a proud, passionate man.

273
00:13:14,370 --> 00:13:16,790
If you go running out on him again,

274
00:13:16,790 --> 00:13:18,600
you're only gonna get, like,

275
00:13:18,600 --> 00:13:22,220
three or four more chances before you are history.

276
00:13:24,370 --> 00:13:26,070
Come on, she came back.

277
00:13:26,070 --> 00:13:27,190
This is good news.

278
00:13:27,190 --> 00:13:28,490
You should celebrate.

279
00:13:28,490 --> 00:13:30,770
I don't want to celebrate.

280
00:13:36,340 --> 00:13:37,650
Not even a little?

281
00:13:37,650 --> 00:13:39,660
I mean... we could have a pants party.

282
00:13:39,660 --> 00:13:41,380
Go put some on.

283
00:13:42,090 --> 00:13:43,330
Why would I want her number?

284
00:13:43,330 --> 00:13:45,180
I don't want anything to do with this woman.

285
00:13:45,180 --> 00:13:46,860
- Oh, come on, Raj... - No, you don't get it.

286
00:13:46,860 --> 00:13:48,710
I want nothing to do with any woman.

287
00:13:49,540 --> 00:13:51,000
My heart is stone.

288
00:13:53,040 --> 00:13:54,890
From now on, I'm a monk.

289
00:13:54,890 --> 00:13:57,250
I renounce all worldly pleasures.

290
00:13:57,960 --> 00:13:59,760
Except for lobster.

291
00:14:00,910 --> 00:14:02,650
And garlic butter.

292
00:14:04,200 --> 00:14:05,500
Boy, I want to tell you it's her loss,

293
00:14:05,500 --> 00:14:07,380
but you are not making it easy.

294
00:14:09,900 --> 00:14:12,790
You're-you're a good friend for trying to help, but...

295
00:14:13,350 --> 00:14:14,800
I've made my choice.

296
00:14:15,850 --> 00:14:17,100
All right.

297
00:14:17,100 --> 00:14:21,010
- Well, I'll see you around. - See you.

298
00:14:21,520 --> 00:14:24,100
Oh, wait-- take her number.

299
00:14:24,100 --> 00:14:25,680
I don't want the temptation.

300
00:14:25,680 --> 00:14:27,220
Okay.

301
00:14:27,840 --> 00:14:30,610
I must be strong so I don't stray from my true purpose:

302
00:14:30,610 --> 00:14:33,290
the study of the universe.

303
00:14:35,440 --> 00:14:36,740
All right.

304
00:14:43,480 --> 00:14:45,710
Thanks for ruining lobster for me.

305
00:14:51,170 --> 00:14:51,970
Wait!

306
00:14:51,970 --> 00:14:53,440
Give me the number!

307
00:14:55,410 --> 00:14:56,650
Give me the number!

308
00:14:56,650 --> 00:14:58,490
Give me the number!

309
00:14:59,920 --> 00:15:03,260
So, Amy, what's going on with your addiction study?

310
00:15:03,260 --> 00:15:06,300
Sadly, I'm no longer associated with that project.

311
00:15:06,300 --> 00:15:07,540
Why? What happened?

312
00:15:07,540 --> 00:15:09,580
Typical bureaucratic nonsense.

313
00:15:09,580 --> 00:15:11,950
You can get animals addicted to a harmful substance,

314
00:15:11,950 --> 00:15:13,280
you can dissect their brains,

315
00:15:13,280 --> 00:15:15,110
but you throw their own feces back at them

316
00:15:15,110 --> 00:15:17,860
and suddenly you're "unprofessional."

317
00:15:19,710 --> 00:15:21,160
I'm sorry...

318
00:15:21,910 --> 00:15:23,520
...that I asked.

319
00:15:25,160 --> 00:15:27,750
All right, let's get this stupid play over with.

320
00:15:27,750 --> 00:15:28,740
Uh, hang on.

321
00:15:28,740 --> 00:15:29,980
Empty your pockets.

322
00:15:29,980 --> 00:15:30,760
Why?

323
00:15:30,760 --> 00:15:31,550
You know why.

324
00:15:31,550 --> 00:15:33,090
The Nintendo DS.

325
00:15:37,720 --> 00:15:39,390
And the PSP.

326
00:15:43,930 --> 00:15:45,520
Now the Gameboy.

327
00:15:45,520 --> 00:15:48,020
Aw, for Pete's sake.

328
00:15:49,020 --> 00:15:49,930
Can we go now?

329
00:15:49,930 --> 00:15:51,830
Well, is that all of it?

330
00:16:01,360 --> 00:16:02,920
Just set it down.

331
00:16:05,010 --> 00:16:07,050
Just so you know, this is not a stupid play.

332
00:16:07,050 --> 00:16:09,790
A Streetcar Named Desire is an American classic.

333
00:16:09,790 --> 00:16:11,760
It's about streetcars?

334
00:16:11,760 --> 00:16:15,040
Oh, great. I won't need this.

335
00:16:28,750 --> 00:16:29,940
Just a sec.

336
00:16:30,410 --> 00:16:32,130
Oh, who says "just a sec"?

337
00:16:32,130 --> 00:16:33,690
I hate myself!

338
00:16:38,690 --> 00:16:40,030
Hello.

339
00:16:40,030 --> 00:16:41,010
Hi.

340
00:16:41,010 --> 00:16:42,570
Uh, would you like to come in?

341
00:16:42,570 --> 00:16:45,540
Oh, no, I can't stay.

342
00:16:47,190 --> 00:16:49,030
I just wanted to say...

343
00:16:49,030 --> 00:16:51,380
I'm sorry for running out of the coffee shop.

344
00:16:51,380 --> 00:16:52,720
That wasn't cool.

345
00:16:52,720 --> 00:16:54,060
So, uh...

346
00:16:54,060 --> 00:16:55,630
Yeah.

347
00:16:56,210 --> 00:16:57,600
I'm sorry.

348
00:16:58,540 --> 00:16:59,730
Wait.

349
00:17:01,450 --> 00:17:04,490
Can you at least tell me what went wrong?

350
00:17:04,490 --> 00:17:06,460
It's okay. I can take anything.

351
00:17:06,460 --> 00:17:07,610
Unless it's something I did,

352
00:17:07,610 --> 00:17:08,620
or said, or am.

353
00:17:08,620 --> 00:17:10,390
'Cause those are, like, my buttons.

354
00:17:12,780 --> 00:17:15,060
No, it's not any of that.

355
00:17:15,060 --> 00:17:16,220
It's just...

356
00:17:17,030 --> 00:17:18,560
I kind of have a hard time

357
00:17:18,560 --> 00:17:20,780
around people I don't know.

358
00:17:20,780 --> 00:17:22,030
Really?

359
00:17:22,030 --> 00:17:22,930
Then what were you doing

360
00:17:22,930 --> 00:17:24,950
at the comic book store that night?

361
00:17:25,520 --> 00:17:27,720
I've been trying to force myself into situations

362
00:17:27,720 --> 00:17:29,810
that I'm not comfortable with.

363
00:17:29,810 --> 00:17:31,930
I saw the flyer in the store window,

364
00:17:31,930 --> 00:17:34,060
and I made myself go in.

365
00:17:34,060 --> 00:17:35,970
I don't even like comic books.

366
00:17:35,970 --> 00:17:37,270
Yeah, me neither.

367
00:17:37,270 --> 00:17:38,380
Then what were you doing there?

368
00:17:38,380 --> 00:17:40,160
I lied. I love them.

369
00:17:42,550 --> 00:17:44,740
I only said that so you'd go out with me.

370
00:17:44,740 --> 00:17:46,770
Oh, you don't want to do that.

371
00:17:46,770 --> 00:17:48,600
I'm kind of broken.

372
00:17:48,600 --> 00:17:49,750
That's great.

373
00:17:49,750 --> 00:17:50,880
I'm broken, too.

374
00:17:50,880 --> 00:17:51,830
Oh, no, you're not.

375
00:17:51,830 --> 00:17:52,890
Oh, I totally am.

376
00:17:52,890 --> 00:17:54,330
If it wasn't for this beer,

377
00:17:54,330 --> 00:17:55,880
I couldn't even talk to you right now.

378
00:17:55,880 --> 00:17:56,900
I'm a wreck.

379
00:17:56,900 --> 00:17:59,980
There are many things seriously wrong with me.

380
00:18:01,140 --> 00:18:02,880
And not quirks, either.

381
00:18:02,880 --> 00:18:08,120
Like... diagnosable psychological problems.

382
00:18:09,560 --> 00:18:11,220
Maybe brain damage.

383
00:18:14,370 --> 00:18:16,960
Well, how do I know you're not just saying that?

384
00:18:18,460 --> 00:18:20,410
Go out with me on one date,

385
00:18:20,410 --> 00:18:23,630
and I promise you, you'll see.

386
00:18:24,870 --> 00:18:26,090
Okay.

387
00:18:26,510 --> 00:18:27,850
Text me.

388
00:18:27,850 --> 00:18:29,230
Bye.

389
00:18:29,970 --> 00:18:31,060
You won't regret it.

390
00:18:31,060 --> 00:18:33,720
I'm the most pathetic guy you've ever met.

391
00:18:35,450 --> 00:18:37,510
And that, boys and girls...

392
00:18:37,510 --> 00:18:39,210
is how it's done.

393
00:18:46,410 --> 00:18:48,560
You love her very much, don't you?

394
00:18:49,250 --> 00:18:50,710
Yes.

395
00:18:50,710 --> 00:18:53,720
I think you have a great capacity for devotion.

396
00:18:54,230 --> 00:18:56,700
You'll be lonely when she passes on, won't you?

397
00:18:58,800 --> 00:19:00,850
I understand what that is.

398
00:19:00,850 --> 00:19:01,800
To be lonely?

399
00:19:01,800 --> 00:19:03,020
She's pretty good, huh?

400
00:19:03,020 --> 00:19:04,700
She is.

401
00:19:04,700 --> 00:19:08,560
But when do they get to the part about streetcars?

402
00:19:11,630 --> 00:19:14,640
...when I was a very young girl.

403
00:19:14,640 --> 00:19:17,750
When I was 16 years old, I made the discovery...

404
00:19:18,700 --> 00:19:20,080
love.

405
00:19:21,520 --> 00:19:22,300
All at once,

406
00:19:22,300 --> 00:19:25,460
and much, much too completely.

407
00:19:26,110 --> 00:19:28,110
It was like you suddenly turned a blinding light

408
00:19:28,110 --> 00:19:31,660
on something that had always been half a shadow.

409
00:19:32,130 --> 00:19:35,290
That's how it struck the world for me.

410
00:19:36,250 --> 00:19:38,340
But I was unlucky.

411
00:19:39,010 --> 00:19:40,610
Deluded.

412
00:19:40,610 --> 00:19:41,700
She's remarkable.

413
00:19:41,700 --> 00:19:43,150
She really is.

414
00:19:43,150 --> 00:19:44,930
Our Penny's a star.

415
00:19:46,010 --> 00:19:48,360
How can she remember all those lines,

416
00:19:48,360 --> 00:19:50,000
but as a waitress, she can't remember

417
00:19:50,000 --> 00:19:52,930
"no tomato" on my hamburger?

